# the argument of aquinas-evil-objection.md by rule (phil/skeleton): connectives from the parse, an atom to each clause
atom	objection_1_seem	Objection 1 It seems that God does not exist because if one of two contraries be infinite the other would be altogether destroyed
atom	mean_infinite_goodness(x)	x: but means that He is infinite goodness
